---
import Layout from '../../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import galacide_logo from '../../assets/galacide_logo.png';
import galacide_1 from '../../assets/galacide_1.jpg';
import galacide_2 from '../../assets/galacide_2.jpg';
import galacide_3 from '../../assets/galacide_3.jpg';	
---

<Layout
	title="Portfolio - Galacide (2015)"
	description="Portfolio - Galacide"
	pubDate={new Date('September 11 2026')}
	/*heroImage="../src/assets/galacide_logo.png"*/
>

	<center>
		<Image src={galacide_logo} alt="Galacide" width="400" />
	</center>

	<p>
		Galacide is a cross between a puzzle game and a traditional space shoot-em-up. The player controls a ship that 
		can shoot down enemies, which drop "scrap" that must be picked up to clear the "bits" that block the player 
		from proressing forward. Each ship has unique weapons and abilities.
	</p>

	<center>
		<iframe
			width="560"
			height="315"
			src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/olneAvBf6Og"
			title="YouTube video"
			frameborder="0"
			allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
			allowfullscreen>
		</iframe>
	</center>

	<p>
		While working on Galacide, I served as the lead designer, as well as doing duties including programming, level 
		design, visual effects, sound effects, and enemy and boss scripting. The game was built using the Unreal engine.
	</p>

	<center>
		<Image src={galacide_1} alt="Galacide" />
	</center>

	<br/>

	<center>
		<Image src={galacide_2} alt="Galacide" />
	</center>

	<br/>

	<center>
		<Image src={galacide_3} alt="Galacide" />
	</center>


</Layout>
